From 450735aa468eff1936344324537d39aaf717efab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:57:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 115/120] gui: run "at machine startup" jobs once per boot, in
 the service

Jobs set to "Also run at machine startup" were run by the GUI process,
from App.startup, every time the window opened: at every login and every
launch. Each run went to the service through the API, past the service's
own guard against running a job twice, so it could run next to the
service's scheduled run of the same job. The GUI also tried to record the
run in the service's state directory and was denied.

The service now runs them when it starts, and only when the machine
booted less than 15 minutes ago (systemUptime), so restarting the service
does not start a backup either. The GUI no longer runs them.

Reported in rdemsystems/NimbusBackupClient#12.
